On Oct 6, 2010, at 9:54 AM, Ewan Dunbar wrote:

> 
> There are two things going on. First, Doulos is a TrueType font. The default screen plot device supports TTFs, but, at least on non-Windows systems, the pdf and ps devices do not. Second, even if you could get the font to work, the pdf device chokes on Unicode, which was the original problem. (To see this, try using a non-TTF font that supports the glyph using the pdf device.) The cairo_pdf device (and other cairo devices) will support both TTF and Unicode.
